  "Question": "There are 10 people in the Chinese language group and 9 in the mathematics group. 4 people participate in both groups. Counting each person only once, how many people are there in total? Calculate: \\(10+9-4=?\\)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "15",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The sum \\(10+9\\) counts the 4 people in both groups twice. Subtracting 4 removes their extra count, leaving each person in either group counted once: \\(10+9-4=15\\). There are \\(15\\) people in total.",
